<onlyinclude>'''Senescence''' is age-associated deterioration in biological function, or, in cellular biology, a distinct state in which a cell typically stops dividing persistently while remaining metabolically active. These meanings are related but are not identical.

== Explanation ==
An organism may become more vulnerable to disease as it ages. Some cells enter a non-dividing state after damage or stress and can influence nearby tissue. Cellular senescence can help with processes such as wound repair or limiting damaged-cell proliferation, but its accumulation can also contribute to disease. Aging is not caused by cellular senescence alone.

